findings.body:
In `testCheckSystemThemeChanges`, the "Select Light mode" step was changed from `lightThemeView` to `darkThemeView`, but the assertion still expects `"1"` and the variable is still named `lightIsSelected`. After selecting Light, the dark button's value should be `"0"`, so this assertion fails on the first step and the rest of the test never runs. The fix is to read `lightThemeView` again. The PR's own description ("aligned with the steps") suggests the intent was to add or change a step, not to swap the identifier.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/firefox-ios-tests/Tests/XCUITests/DisplaySettingsTests.swift" lines="46-59"}

::suggestion{file="firefox-ios/firefox-ios-tests/Tests/XCUITests/DisplaySettingsTests.swift" lines="53-54"}
        let lightIsSelected = app.buttons[AccessibilityIdentifiers.Settings.Appearance.lightThemeView].value
        XCTAssertEqual(lightIsSelected as? String, "1")

The mapping is in ::file{file="firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Settings/AppearanceSettings/ThemeOptionView.swift"}: light maps to `lightThemeView`, dark to `darkThemeView`.

The `checkCopiedUrl()` call was removed from `testClipboard`, so the test no longer checks that the copied URL matches what is in the browser before it pastes into a new tab. The PR description only covers deleted test methods and a new test, so this removal is undocumented. `checkCopiedUrl()` is now only referenced in a commented-out block in `testClipboardPasteAndGo`, so it is dead code in practice. Either restore the call or delete the helper and explain the reason in the PR. A test that copies and then pastes without checking the pasteboard can pass even when the copy failed.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/firefox-ios-tests/Tests/XCUITests/ClipBoardTests.swift" lines="66-72"}

The current test body reads: `openURL`, `waitUntilPageLoad`, `checkUrl`, `copyUrl`, then `createNewTab` and the paste assertion.
